      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm still a little uneasy about it though. i was reading an article earlier that mentioned serotonin syndrome is a real thing if you mix SSRIs like sertraline with dextromethorphan. it sounded pretty serious, like it could cause confusion or high blood pressure. are you absolutely sure there's no risk for me? i'd hate to end up in the hospital just because i wanted to stop coughing.",
